The once-per-run diversity arm is fixed and verified. Recording three things
that the code alone does not say.

Two decorative-test failures on my own work. The first version tested a
hand-written mirror of the rule, to dodge the memory watchdog that refuses
importing arc_competition_agent, and two mutations of the real code survived
because a mirror passes every mutation of what it mirrors. Repaired by
extracting the rule to a light module. A fifth mutation discarding the return
value then still survived, because nothing asserted the agent stores it, and
discarding it converts a once-per-level reset into an every-tick reset. I
briefed both subagents that a mutation must bite the call site rather than a
constant, then committed that error twice in twenty minutes.

Provenance defect. git log --diff-filter=A shows both source files were
introduced by conductor checkpoint commits, not by mine, so my commit carrying
the explanation holds only the spec. The conductor's checkpoint path swept my
in-progress tree; it respects no declared scope and runs no hooks. The code
works and is on main, the provenance is wrong, and the lints did not run on it.
Not repaired by rewriting a published commit, which would be worse than the
wrong authorship; this record is the repair.

Whole-tree collection is 61,976 with 4 errors, all pre-existing: three modules
never committed, and one deliberately quarantined by 06cbad7cdd.

