+## 2026-09-05 06:30Z — the once-per-run arm is FIXED, and the conductor took the commit
+
+REQ-ARC-WMTE-7040 shipped. `python/carnot/agentic/arc_arm_eligibility.py:restore_arm_eligibility`
+restores the explorer's operator-configured diversity baseline when the level advances, called
+from `_observe_trajectory` BEFORE the snapshot is built. The force-diversity arm is now eligible
+once per LEVEL rather than once per RUN.
+
+Fixed on main, not on the unmerged round-two branch, because the bug predates that branch and
+should not wait on a merge decision.
+
+Two properties carry their own mutation, because both are ways to "fix" it wrongly:
+
+- It restores the OPERATOR BASELINE, never a bare `False`. A run started with
+  `CARNOT_ARC_EXPLORE_DIVERSITY=1` asked for diversity throughout; switching it off at a level-up
+  would be a worse defect than the original.
+- It runs BEFORE the snapshot. A restore the supervisor cannot see on the same tick is one it
+  acts on a window late.
+
+### Two decorative-test failures on my own work, recorded because the method is the point
+
+**First: the tests measured a mirror, not the code.** To dodge the per-test memory watchdog — it
+refuses the half-gigabyte import of `arc_competition_agent` — the first version tested a
+hand-written copy of the rule. Two mutations of the REAL code survived, because a mirror passes
+every mutation of the thing it mirrors. Repaired by extracting the rule into its own light module
+so a test can import the real function. That is the same repair pattern used for
+`arc_run_envelope` earlier tonight, and the same reason.
+
+**Second: nothing asserted the agent STORES the return value.** A mutation assigning the result to
+a throwaway still passed everything. Discarding it leaves `_last_supervised_level` at None, so
+`level != last_level` is always true and the once-per-level reset silently becomes an every-tick
+reset — which would undo an arm the supervisor had just fired. A test for the assignment was
+added and that mutation now fails. Final state: 8 tests, 5 of 5 mutations RED.
+
+I briefed both subagents that a mutation must bite the CALL SITE and not just a constant. I then
+committed that exact error twice in twenty minutes. The discipline works; the reason it works is
+that it catches the author.
+
+### PROVENANCE DEFECT: the conductor committed my code under its own name
+
+`git log --diff-filter=A` shows the two source files were introduced not by my commit but by:
+
+- `50a8d2e960 [conductor] Checkpoint: preserve uncommitted work from interrupted run` —
+  `arc_arm_eligibility.py`
+- `ed8fe9134f [conductor] In-process docs for Exact minimal constraint-intervention pair fixture` —
+  the test file
+
+My own commit `c17ec611aa`, whose message explains the bug and the fix, therefore carries **only
+the spec**. The conductor's checkpoint path swept my in-progress working tree, which is the
+hazard already recorded in the memory directory as
+`feedback_checkpoint_commit_bypasses_claims_and_hooks`: that path does not respect a declared
+scope and does not run the hooks.
+
+Consequences, stated rather than smoothed over:
+
+1. The code is on main and works. Verified: module tracked, `HEAD` carries both the import and
+   the call, 8 tests green.
+2. The provenance is wrong. `git log` on those files names conductor tasks that had nothing to do
+   with this change. A future reader tracing the fix will land in an unrelated commit message.
+3. The code never passed pre-commit on its own commit. `ruff format` was run by hand, but the
+   lints that would have run did not.
+
+**Not repaired by rewriting history.** Rewriting a published commit to correct authorship is worse
+than the wrong authorship, and the never-prune doctrine says the record explains rather than
+erases. This entry is the explanation.
+
+### Whole-tree collection: 4 errors, none new
+
+`pytest tests --collect-only` reports 61,976 collected with 4 errors. Three are the known
+`experiment_6814/6819/6828` files whose modules were never committed. The fourth,
+`tests/quarantine/test_experiment_4058_...`, is DELIBERATELY quarantined — commit `06cbad7cdd`
+moved it there to stop it poisoning the pre-test gate. Nothing here is new and nothing is mine.
+
